        "geology": "The site is located over the Alter-do-Chão geological formation, of Cretaceous age.",
        "hydrology": "The hydrology if formed by a dense network of streams mostly from first to forth orders, dissecting the terrains and forming a complex undulating topography of plateaus incised by valleys. Valleys are permanently ot seasonally waterlogged, and stream flooding is irregular and of short duration (maximum of hours).",
        "soils": "Soils are generally poor in nutrients (mostly less than 1 cmol.kg of exchangeable cations). Plateaus have clayey latossols and valleys sandy podzols, slopes have soils in between.",
        "vegetation": "Forest is classified as dense tropical moist forest, around 32 m tall, with emergent trees up to 55 m. Tree diversity is very high, with 1200 sp document in one of the sub-sites for which there is a near complete flora, but the total number may reach 2000 tree sp over the 3 sub-sites."
      },
